# Bumping a schema revision touches four places

Per [CONFIGURATION_UI.md](../../docs/design/CONFIGURATION_UI.md), a worker owns
its configuration vocabulary and the UI refetches when `schema_revision`
changes. Adding or removing a property means bumping the revision, and the
revision string appears in more than one file. Missing one leaves the UI or the
tests disagreeing with the worker.

When changing a schema, update all of:

1. The worker's schema and its `set_schema_revision` calls, in both
   `get_config_schema` and `apply_config`.
2. The daemon's static fallback in `SimEngine::get_config_schema`, which serves
   sources that have no worker.
3. The revision assertions in `tests/protocol/test_daemon_e2e.py`.
4. The status section of [docs/design/README.md](../../docs/design/README.md).

Never reuse a revision string for a changed shape. Existing revisions stay
valid: a worker that reports `camera.gstreamer/1` must keep meaning what it
meant, because on-disk presets reference it.

Guard optional properties in tests. `capture_mode` is only advertised when the
device reports usable modes, so assert on it conditionally or CI without a
camera fails.
